{"name":"Portage","hex":"#8b98d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Portage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A community in Cape Breton Regional Municipality, on Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia, Canada.","A settlement in Prince Edward Island, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Portage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Portage","blocks":[{"text":"Portage or portaging is the practice of carrying water craft or cargo over land, either around an obstacle in a river, or between two bodies of water. A path where items are regularly carried between bodies of water is also called a portage. The term comes from French, where porter means \"to carry\", as in \"portable\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Portage-prospector.jpg/330px-Portage-prospector.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portage","wikidata":"Q120638097"},{"title":"Portage (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Portage is a package management system originally created for and used by Gentoo Linux and also by ChromeOS and Calculate among others. Portage is based on the concept of ports collections. Gentoo is sometimes referred to as a meta-distribution due to the extreme flexibility of Portage, which makes it operating-system-independent. The Gentoo/Alt project was concerned with using Portage to manage other operating systems, such as BSDs, macOS and Solaris. The most notable of these implementations is the Gentoo/FreeBSD project."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Portage-oppdatering.png/330px-Portage-oppdatering.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portage_(software)","wikidata":"Q908542"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Photograph_of_Canoe_Rest_on_Smoke_Lake_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128454.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_Canoe_Rest_on_Smoke_Lake_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128454.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Photograph_of_Canoe_Rest_on_Smoke_Lake_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128454.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_Canoe_Rest_on_Smoke_Lake_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128454.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canoe rest along a portage trail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotograph_of_Canoe_Rest_on_Smoke_Lake_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128454.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Photograph_of_Railroad_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128318.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_Railroad_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128318.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Photograph_of_Railroad_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128318.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_Railroad_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128318.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Small railway portage in the U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotograph_of_Railroad_Portage_-_NARA_-_2128318.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg/500px-Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg/1280px-Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg/500px-Diolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paved section of the Diolkos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiolkos%2C_Western_End._Pic_04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/